course: dictionary
lesson: 6879
title: Overlordship and who holds power
level: primary-6
stars: 3
explain: Some words are built from parts you already know. An overlord is a ruler who has power over other lords or kings. Add -ship, and overlordship names that power or position: being the overlord.
explain: «Moscow was a small principality, a land ruled by a prince, under the overlordship of the Golden Horde in 1337.» The clue is «under»: the prince of Moscow had to answer to a stronger ruler. So overlordship is the power the Horde held over Moscow.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Under the power of the ruler over other lords» still makes sense, so you have it right. Now read the next clue: «Ivan III stopped paying tribute to the Horde in 1480.» Stopping a payment shows that the payment had been owed, so overlordship also gave the overlord the right to collect it.
fact: Overlordship means the power or position of an overlord.
fact: An overlord is a ruler who has power over other lords or kings.
fact: The ending -ship often names a position or state, as in friendship or leadership.
fact: Tribute means a yearly payment made by a ruled land to its overlord.
fact: «Moscow» was under the overlordship of the Golden Horde in 1337; by 1480, «Ivan III» had stopped paying tribute to the Horde.
exercise: «Moscow was under the overlordship of the Golden Horde in 1337.» What does overlordship mean? | A big feast held in a castle | *The power or position of a ruler over other lords or kings | A fast horse used for carrying messages | A kind of hat worn by princes
exercise: Find and copy the word from «Ivan III stopped paying tribute to the Horde in 1480.» that means a yearly payment made to an overlord. | Horde | paying | *tribute | Ivan
exercise: Which word is made from overlord with the ending -ship, showing a position of power? | *overlordship | overload | lordly | overlook
test: «A king might accept another king's overlordship.» What does this tell you? | The two kings were best friends and equal in every way | The first king gave the second king a gift | *The first king accepted that the second king had power over him | The first king went to live in another country
test: «Ivan III stopped paying tribute.» What does tribute mean? | A prize for winning a race | A song sung at a royal wedding | *A yearly payment made by a ruled land to its overlord | A gift given on a birthday
exam: What does the clue «stopped paying tribute» tell you about the Horde's overlordship of Moscow? | That Moscow had no prince | That Moscow was free from all rule | *That the Horde had been collecting yearly payments from Moscow | That the Horde was kind and never asked for anything
